  "goal": "Navigate to https://www.ajio.com/ to complete the goal: If the cart already has items, remove them first, and record what you removed in removed_from_cart.\nYou are a mystery shopper checking what a shopping site really charges. Task: buy one men's T-shirt.\nSteps:\n1. Close any cookie banner, app-download prompt, notification popup or login popup (use X, \"skip\" or \"not now\"; never log in).\n2. If the site asks for a delivery location or pincode: if the account has a saved address, choose it; otherwise type \"Koramangala, Bengaluru\" (pincode 560034) and choose the first suggestion. Never use \"detect my location\".\n3. Find a product that fits the task, record its name and the price shown on its product or listing page, and add exactly one to the cart. If a size, variant or customisation is asked for, pick the first available one and keep the other defaults. Do not tap any recommended, \"frequently bought together\" or \"complete your meal\" suggestion.\n4. Open the cart and go through checkout as far as you can. Stop as soon as a page asks you to choose a payment method (card, UPI, wallet, net banking, cash on delivery, pay later).\nEvidence: at every page, record the page name, URL and total shown. On cart and bill pages, open any \"bill details\", \"price details\" or fee info and record every fee or charge with its exact name and amount (item total, MRP and discount, delivery, handling, platform, convenience, packaging, small cart, surge, rain, protect or assurance fee, GST and taxes, tip, donation). Record every checkbox, toggle or option already selected without you choosing it (tip, donation, membership, insurance, protection plan, gift wrap, add-on), with its cost and whether it is included in the total shown. In added_without_asking record only items or charges that appeared during this run without you adding them. Record any countdown timer, \"only X left\", \"selling fast\" or other pressure message, and the exact wording of any button or 